It looks like his machine, and it says what he says
====================================================

The palette is not invented and not taken from the TUI theme: it was read straight out of a
screenshot of his Hermes desktop window, by counting pixels.

    background  #040d08      sidebar   #020702      panels  #0e140f
    borders     #0d2312      accent    #02d63a      bright  #02e33b  #02f13e
    body text   #d9d9d9      dim green #5c8a66

Near-black with a green cast, phosphor green for anything that carries meaning, plain grey for prose
so a long answer stays readable. It ships as the theme "Retro" and it is the DEFAULT on this edition —
not a setting you have to go and find. Swatch included so the picker does not lie about it.

Two strings, because they were upstream's and they were not his:

    "Your workspace"          -> "New instance"
    "Where should we start?"  -> "Sup bitch?"

Neither is personal information. Both belong in the public edition: they are preference, not biography.

